  "id": "health-locus-of-control",
  "term": "health locus of control",
  "definition": "Health locus of control is a person’s expectation about what determines health outcomes. It describes whether someone sees health as mainly influenced by their own actions and characteristics or by outside forces such as chance, fate, luck, or other people.",
